This is certainly true. The FS is stable enough for my use, but I won't
use it for anything except temporary partitions (/tmp /var/tmp
/usr/portage) because if I need to resize I have to recreate. It makes
LVM so pointless.

I have also seen people mention that the lack of resizing capabilities
is a major roadblock for them to adopt reiser4.

I can completely understand working out bugs first; however, apart from
that I believe it should be given quite high priority.

